The attached image illustrates Nano-11's role in antigen targeting and retention. Figure 6a (Image A) demonstrates that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) exhibit the highest CD86 expression among antigen-presenting cells in the draining lymph node, indicating their enhanced activation. Figure 6b (Image B) further characterizes OVA-positive MigDCs, showing they are predominantly CD11b+ DCs and monocyte-derived dendritic cells after Nano-11 adjuvanted immunization. Figure 6c (Image C) shows in vivo imaging results, confirming that Nano-11, similar to aluminum hydroxide (AH), significantly prolongs antigen retention at the injection site for up to 7 days compared to soluble OVA, supporting its efficacy as a vaccine adjuvant by facilitating sustained antigen presentation.